     <svg:title>TexMaths</svg:title>
     <svg:desc>12§display§Q=CV§png§600§FALSE§</svg:desc>
    </draw:frame><text:span text:style-name="T44">). </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T45">Field effect transistors (</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44">FETs</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T45">)</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T44"> take advantage of this physical phenomenon: as opposed to a BJT, where there is a non-negligible current which flows into the device from the base, a FET attempts to isolate it’s control terminal from the active device. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P27"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Frame7" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6.3846in" draw:z-index="14">
