      <svg:title>TexMaths</svg:title>
      <svg:desc>12§display§V_1§svg§600§FALSE§</svg:desc>
     </draw:frame></text:span>, which in effect, adjusts the resistance through the device. </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P30">A common type of FET is the MOSFET (Metal-oxide Semiconductor FET). </text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P31">When a voltage is applied to the gate, a large negative charge buildup forms across the channel (from Source to Drain), and if the voltage difference from Gate to Source exceeds our device’s inherent threshold voltage, a conventional current from Drain to Source is formed. It should be noted that, implied by the capacitave nature of the device, the <text:span text:style-name="T10">width</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T48"> to </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T10">length</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T48"> ratio of the channel is directly proportional to the current that this device can conduct through it. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T49">We will neglect a discussion on the I-V characteristics of a MOSFET. It should be noted that MOSFETs are voltage controlled devices, no current flows into the gate during normal operation at steady state (i.e. the gate capacitance is not changing). Typically, MOSFETs have a faster switching speed than BJTs, as in, the channel in a MOSFET can cut off the short between the Source and Drain at a rate which is faster than the rate of recombination in the body of a BJT. </text:span></text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P5" text:outline-level="2">IGBTs</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32">The IGBT <text:span text:style-name="T50">can be thought of as a combination of </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51">a MOSFET and a BJT. At a high level, IGBTs use a capacitave gating technique similar to a MOSFET, but unlike a MOSFET it has a </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T52">pn</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T51"> junction at the drain side. We’ll see how we realize these benefits as we study the topology of this device.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P32"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr3" draw:name="Frame4" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6.9252in" draw:z-index="18">
     <draw:text-box fo:min-height="2.9256in">
