        </draw:image>
       </draw:frame>Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure8" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">14</text:sequence>: On-state current flow paths in an IGBT <text:span text:style-name="T56">(Mohan)</text:span></text:p>
     </draw:text-box>
    </draw:frame></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P37">A substantial amount of electrons flow into the <text:span text:style-name="T10">n-</text:span> drain drift region, which induces a large amount of holes to enter the drain drift region as well, via drift and diffusion. <text:span text:style-name="T57">In this configuration, our junction </text:span><text:soft-page-break/><text:span text:style-name="T57">between the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T58">p</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"> and </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T58">n-</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"> region operates as a collector for the diffusing holes, our </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T58">p+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"> region acts like an emitter, and our base is the </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T58">n-</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"> drift region. Figure </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"><text:sequence-ref text:reference-format="value" text:ref-name="refFigure7">13</text:sequence-ref></text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"><text:s/>demonstrates the full picture: we operate a voltage-controlled gate, which provides an impulse current that triggers t</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T59">h</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57">e </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">logical </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T58">pnp</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">structure </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T57">to enter forward active mode, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T6">following similar characteristics.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P38"><text:span text:style-name="T55">Th</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60">e </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T61">n+</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T60"> </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T55">buffer layer is not explicitly necessary. The presence of it indicates that this is a punch-through IGBT. </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T62">Including this region means that we have a thinner potential barrier, which drops our on-state losses. However, this means our reverse-blocking ability is diminished, and our device will only work in forward biased mode (</text:span><text:span text:style-name="T63"><draw:frame text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:y="-0.1138in" draw:z-index="11" draw:name="Shape4" draw:style-name="gr1" draw:text-style-name="P19" svg:width="0.5252in" svg:height="0.1398in">
      <draw:image draw:mime-type="image/svg+xml">
